## Report: `DET.APP.PERSISTENT_CHROME` rule page

Wrote the handbook page from:
- Source rule: `docs/design/ux-audit/deterministic-design-rules.md#det-app-persistent-chrome`
- Implementation: `design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-app-persistent-chrome.check.js`
- Schema: `RULE_PAGE_SCHEMA.md`
- KS patterns: `Msm` museum studio shell, `data-shell-region`, `nav-section-label`, `forge-card`, `ks-wizard-flow__session-list`, etc.

### Page contents

| Section | Summary |
|---------|---------|
| **Purpose** | Route-crawl check: fingerprint `header`/`nav`/`aside`/`footer` and `[data-shell-region]` outside `main`; compare across routes when persistence is promised |
| **Passing signals** | Stable regions, ids, `data-ks-hash`, global nav link sets; only `main` swaps |
| **Failing signals** | `missing-region`, `nav-drift`, `hash-drift`, `promised-no-regions` |
| **Before example** | `/settings` route with route-local header nav + missing side rail (nav-drift + missing-region) |
| **After example** | Stable `Msm` shell with `data-shell-regions`, persistent `header`/`nav`, route content only in `main` |
| **Evidence and remediation** | `appPersistentChromeReport.violations[]`, paired screenshots, 5-step fix order |
| **Related rules** | 7 linked rules (landmarks, chrome boundary, breadcrumb, dedup, focus trap, AI workflow/density) |

